ed only; not a new Lean declaration or independently replayed proof. The word is fixed before n tends to infinity. The second moment is the quantum second moment averaged over disorder, not only the squared conditional energy expectation. No uniform rate over depth or angles is asserted.","citation_ids":["fggz2022_fixed_depth"],"evidence_ids":["concentration_source_warrant_pending"],"id":"circuit.fixed_word_concentration","kind":"claim","label":"Fixed-word SK QAOA first and second measurement moments","locator":"Farhi-Goldstone-Gutmann-Zhou, arXiv:1910.08187v4, section 4 theorem, equations (13)-(14).","source_id":"fggz2022_fixed_depth","statement":"For every fixed finite depth p and fixed real angle vectors gamma and beta, with standard Gaussian SK couplings and the usual plus-state QAOA circuit, let Y_n=H_n(sigma)/n for a computational-basis outcome sigma. Over the joint law of disorder and measurement, E[Y_n] tends to v_p(gamma,beta) and E[Y_n^2] tends to v_p(gamma,beta)^2 as n tends to infinity.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/circuit.fixed_word_concentration","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/circuit.fixed_word_concentration","id":"field:d7d4a0f3518123a72bd76df0aa14bf2bcd6abddbcad3c2ded5a6dbbe2b0cd1cc","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/circuit.fixed_word_concentration","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/assumptions.qaoa_model_and_limits"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/nodes/circuit.one_measurement_near_optimum","id":"sha256:05cd25e48622c61863e237a23bb6df11291711ec1cc1686433b4a62c89a6f0f0/edges